 "When confirming a block, different networks use different rules: some compete by computing power for the right to keep the ledger, while others vote according to holdings and reputation, and the design of the rules directly affects energy consumption and security.",
 "Records on the blockchain are linked in chronological order, and each block contains the fingerprint of the previous one; once a record is written, altering it requires altering all subsequent blocks at the same time, which is practically impossible in a network with many nodes.",
